---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const seo = {
  title: "How to Download & Analyze Your CAMS/KFintech CAS Statement | Arthavi",
  description: "Step-by-step guide to downloading your Consolidated Account Statement (CAS) from CAMS or KFintech. Learn how to parse it locally to track your mutual fund portfolio.",
};
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="cams cas statement download, kfintech cas statement, how to get cas statement, mutual fund statement analysis, parse cas pdf, track mutual funds via cas"
  schema={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "How to Download & Analyze Your CAMS/KFintech CAS Statement",
    "image": "https://arthavi.com/images/og-image.png",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Arthavi"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Arthavi",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://arthavi.com/images/logo.png"
        }
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-02-16",
      "description": "A complete guide to downloading and analyzing your mutual fund history using the CAS statement."
    })}
  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/how-to-download-analyze-cams-cas-statement" }
    ]
  }}
>

    <main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);">
        <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">How to Download & Analyze Your CAMS/KFintech CAS
                Statement</h1>

            <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                Your mutual fund portfolio is likely scattered across apps like Groww, Coin, Kuvera, or directly with
                AMCs. The <strong>Consolidated Account Statement (CAS)</strong> is the single source of truth that ties
                it all together.
            </p>

            <p>In this guide, we'll explain what a CAS is, how to download it for free, and how to use it to audit your
                wealth.</p>

            <div
                style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-surface); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">What is a CAS?</h2>
                <p>A <strong>Consolidated Account Statement (CAS)</strong> is a document issued by depositories
                    (NSDL/CDSL) or RTAs (CAMS/KFintech) that lists:</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Every mutual fund unit you own (across all AMCs).</li>
                    <li>Every stock you hold in your Demat account (if requested).</li>
                    <li>All financial transactions (SIPs, redemptions, dividends).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">It is the "master record" of your financial life.</p>
            </div>

            <h2>Step 1: Request Your Mailback CAS</h2>
            <p>You don't need to log in or create an account. You can request a "Mailback CAS" directly from the RTA
                websites.</p>

            <h3>Option A: Via CAMS Online (Recommended)</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Go to the <a href="https://www.camsonline.com/Investors/Statements/Consolidated-Account-Statement"
                        target="_blank" rel="nofollow">CAMS CAS Request Page</a>.</li>
                <li>Select <strong>"Detailed"</strong> statement type to see transaction history (crucial for XIRR).
                </li>
                <li>Enter your registered <strong>Email</strong> and <strong>PAN</strong>.</li>
                <li>Set a <strong>Password</strong> (you will need this to open the PDF).</li>
                <li>Click Submit.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3>Option B: Via KFintech</h3>
            <ol>
                <li>Visit the <a href="https://mfs.kfintech.com/investor/General/ConsolidatedAccountStatement"
                        target="_blank" rel="nofollow">KFintech CAS Page</a>.</li>
                <li>Choose "Detailed CAS".</li>
                <li>Enter your details and password.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Step 2: Download the PDF</h2>
            <p>Within 10-15 minutes, you will receive an email from <code>donotreply@camsonline.com</code> or KFintech.
            </p>
            <p>Open the email and download the attachment. The password to open the file is the one you set during the
                request (or sometimes your PAN number, check the email instructions).</p>

            <div class="glass-panel" style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--primary-glow);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--primary-glow);">Step 3: Analyze with Arthavi</h2>
                <p>Reading a raw PDF statement is tedious. It's pages and pages of tables.</p>
                <p>Instead, use Arthavi's <strong>secure local parser</strong> to turn that PDF into a powerful
                    dashboard.</p>

                <ol style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <li>Go to <strong><a href="https://app.arthavi.com" style="color: var(--text-head);">Arthavi
                                Dashboard</a></strong>.</li>
                    <li>Click <strong>"Import Investments"</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Select your downloaded PDF file and enter the password.</li>
                </ol>

                <p style="background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.1); padding: 1rem; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.9rem;">
                    <strong>🔒 Security Note:</strong> Arthavi processes this file <em>inside your browser</em>. The
                    file contents are parsed locally on your device, ensuring your financial data remains private.
                </p>

                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                    <a href="https://app.arthavi.com" class="btn btn-primary">Import My Investments</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2>Why You Should Do This Monthly</h2>
            <p>We verify your portfolio against the official RTA records to ensure:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>No Missing Units:</strong> Ensure every SIP installment was actually credited.</li>
                <li><strong>Dividend Checks:</strong> Verify if dividend payouts hit your bank account.</li>
                <li><strong>True XIRR:</strong> Calculate returns based on actual transaction dates, not just current
                    value.</li>
            </ul>

            <p>Stop guessing your net worth. Download your CAS today and see the full picture.</p>

        </article>
    </main>

